X:514
T:Queen Mary's Lamentation. Roose.0514
M:3/4
L:1/8
Q:3/4=40
N:There is a published song of this title published in 1785
N:described 'as sung by Sigr. Tenducci at the Pantheon & Mr. Abel's Concert &c'
N:There is a version of the tune in the same key in the Edward Holmes M. EHo.395
N:It is also in
N:'Aird – Selection of Scotch, English, Irish and Foreign Airs, vol. 4' (1796, No. 52, p. 20)
N:in the key of G.
N:Note 1, final note looks like a grace note, bar would be short without the semiquaver.
N:Tune includes a flattened 7th a mixylodian attribute.
B:John Roose, Manchester 1850
Z:Village Music Project. Rob Lands 2019
