N:NB1) Sic!
N:NB2) Ambiguous. F (grace note)is not marked as sharp or natural in MS.  Is this a carryover sharp (#F) or do
N: we revert to original key signature (=F)?  Assuming here that we revert.
N:NB3) Start of 36-bar final part (part E) is marked in MS with a repeat, but there is no ending repeat mark.
N: Assuming here that the repeat was an error.  Short phrase markers are added here to improve readability,
N: dividing the 36 measure E part into 4 lines of 8 measures, 10 measures, 8 measures and 10 measures,
N: respectfully. (These short phrase marks are not in the original MS.)
N:NB4) Compare part E measure 4 with part E measure 12.  The MS has no accidentals in the latter!  Note
N: also the measures that follow (i.e. 5 and 13) with the same pitch sequence on different rhythms.
N:NB5) This tune uses both staccato dots and staccatissimo wedges.  Current versions of abc2midi ignore
N: staccatissimo wedges, so if wedges are used, they will sound too smooth (legato).  The staccato marks
N:appear in the A part.  Staccatissiomo is used in the B and E parts.
