X:850
T:Cubits Waltz. Roose.0846
T:Cupid's Waltz,aka. Roose.0846
T:Cubitt's Waltz?,aka. Roose.0846
B:J. Roose MS, Manchester 1850
Z:Village Music Project 2019 Eric Conrad
M:3/8
R:waltz
Q:3/8=45
L:1/16
K:F
N:The C part is a variant of the usual tune for "Don't put your muck/trash in my dustbin/backyard;
N:my dustbin's/backyard's full."
N:
N:The tune is appears elsewhere with the title Cupid's Waltz, often starting with the C part.
N:
N:From 1875-1887, William Duncan Cubitt was a dealer in London of musical instruments made to his
N:own specifications.  His clarinets were apparently prized.
N:
N:The title probably does not refer to the unit of measure (cubit), but could refer
N:to a musical member of the Cubitt family.
W:see also: "Cupid's Waltz" (FTB.070) in Fiddler's Tune Book 1. EFDSS.1952
P:A
|: FA | c2c2 Ac | d2d2 fd | cdcBAG | A2F2 FA | \\
