X:856
T:Cotillion. Roose.0852
B:J. Roose MS, Manchester 1850
Z:Village Music Project 2019 Eric Conrad
M:2/4
Q:1/4=110
L:1/16
N:A cotillion (French cotillon -- petticoat) is an early type of square dance.
N:
N:The form is primarily 18th century, with a revival in the 19th century. Cotillions
N:were largely superceded by quadrilles (another early type of square) and by
N:couples dances such as waltzes and mazurkas.
N:
N:NB1) MS marks fine (end) with a fermata.
N:NB2) MS marks da segno (D.S.) with a segno.
P:ABACA
K:D
P:A
|: !segno!abag f2d2 | abag f4 | abag f2d2 | e2c2 "_NB1"!fine!d4 :|
P:B
ABAB A2a2 | gfed e2A2 | ABAB A2a2 | gfed "_NB2"!D.S.!e4 ||
P:C
e2f2e2d2 | e2f2e2d2 | d3ef3e | fef^g "_NB2"!D.S.!a4 ||

